# Lyrics scraping pipeline

Three scripts, one orchestrator.

## Files

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `match-lyrics-nu.js` | Crawl lyrics.nu singer pages, match D1 track names → song URLs |
| `fetch-lyrics-bodies.js` | Crawl each matched song URL, extract lyrics → local JSON |
| `index.js` | Run both in sequence |

## Inputs

| File | Generated by | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `artists.json` | wrangler dump | `[{ artist_id, artist_name }, ...]` |
| `tracks.json` | wrangler dump | `[{ artist_id, track_name }, ...]` |

## Outputs

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `lyrics-matches.json` | per-artist matches: track name → lyrics.nu song URL |
| `lyrics-bodies.json` | per-track: `{ lyrics, bytes, charCount, error }` |

## Run order

### 1. Dump from D1

From `E:\matb3aa-game\music-game-wrangler`:

npx wrangler d1 execute music-game-db --remote --json --command="SELECT id AS artist_id, name AS artist_name FROM artists WHERE tracks_count > 0 ORDER BY name" > ..\server\scripts\lyrics-scrapping\artists.json

npx wrangler d1 execute music-game-db --remote --json --command="SELECT DISTINCT artist_id, name AS track_name FROM tracks WHERE r2_key IS NOT NULL" > ..\server\scripts\lyrics-scrapping\tracks.json

text

### 2. Run the pipeline

From `E:\matb3aa-game\server`:
node scripts/lyrics-scrapping/index.js

text

Or step-by-step:
node scripts/lyrics-scrapping/match-lyrics-nu.js
node scripts/lyrics-scrapping/fetch-lyrics-bodies.js



## Flags

| Flag | Applies to | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `--artist=65` | both scripts | Process only artist 65 |
| `--fresh` | `fetch-lyrics-bodies.js` | Ignore existing `lyrics-bodies.json`, re-fetch everything |

The fetcher resumes by default: on re-run it skips song URLs already present
with a non-error entry in `lyrics-bodies.json`.

## Timing

| Stage | Concurrency | Approx time |
|---|---|---|
| Matching (163 artists) | 4 | 5–20 min |
| Fetching bodies (5,700 tracks) | 4, 400ms delay | 15–25 min |

## notes

- lyrics.nu is scraped politely: `User-Agent` set, 400ms delay, retry with backoff.
- The fetcher tolerates failures: songs that 404 or return no `<section>`
  are stored with an `error` field and can be retried individually.
- Nothing touches D1 in this pipeline. It produces local JSON only.